1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0275-408b1741bd5a:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 120, \"text\": \"Feel the Fire (Family Brown album) Feel the Fire is the tenth studio album by Canadian country music group Family Brown.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0275-408b1741bd5a:d00\", \"start\": 121, \"end\": 239, \"text\": \"It was released in 1985 by RCA Records and was the final album to include founding member Joe Brown, who died in 1986.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0275-408b1741bd5a:d00\", \"start\": 240, \"end\": 435, \"text\": \"The album includes the singles, \\\"Feel the Fire\\\", \\\"What If It's Right\\\", \\\"Wouldn't You Love Us Together Again\\\", and \\\"I Love You More\\\", which all charted on the \\\"RPM\\\" Country Tracks chart in Canada.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0275-408b1741bd5a:d00\", \"start\": 436, \"end\": 549, \"text\": \"The album won the awards for Album of the Year at the 1985 \\\"RPM\\\" Big Country Awards and the 1986 Canadian Country\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0275-408b1741bd5a:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 37, \"text\": \"the Terms of Use and Privacy Policy .\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0275-408b1741bd5a:d01\", \"start\": 38, \"end\": 109, \"text\": \"Wikipedia® is a registered trademark of the Wikimedia Foundation , Inc.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0275-408b1741bd5a:d01\", \"start\": 110, \"end\": 139, \"text\": \", a non-profit organization .\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0275-408b1741bd5a:d01\", \"start\": 140, \"end\": 371, \"text\": \"Privacy policy About Wikipedia Disclaimers Contact Wikipedia Code of Conduct Developers Statistics Cookie statement Mobile view Search Search Toggle the table of contents Feel the Fire ( Family Brown album ) Add languages Add topic\"}, \"D3S1\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0275-408b1741bd5a:d02\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 612, \"text\": \"project English Wikipedia performer Family Brown 1 reference imported from Wikimedia project English Wikipedia record label RCA Records 1 reference imported from Wikimedia project English Wikipedia publication date 1985 1 reference imported from Wikimedia project English Wikipedia Identifiers Freebase ID /m/0ngsvzv 0 references Sitelinks Wikipedia ( 1 entry ) edit enwiki Feel the Fire ( Family Brown album ) Wikibooks ( 0 entries ) edit Wikinews ( 0 entries ) edit Wikiquote ( 0 entries ) edit Wikisource ( 0 entries ) edit Wikiversity ( 0 entries ) edit Wikivoyage ( 0 entries ) edit Wiktionary ( 0 entries )\"}, \"D4S1\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0275-408b1741bd5a:d03\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 140, \"text\": \"Feel the Fire (Jermaine Jackson album) Feel the Fire is the fourth solo album by Jermaine Jackson, and his second post-Jackson 5 solo album.\"}, \"D4S2\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0275-408b1741bd5a:d03\", \"start\": 141, \"end\": 191, \"text\": \"It was dedicated: \\\"to Jai, born January 27, 1977\\\".\"}, \"D4S3\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0275-408b1741bd5a:d03\", \"start\": 192, \"end\": 277, \"text\": \"This is the first album for which Jackson did some producing and writing for himself.\"}, \"D4S4\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0275-408b1741bd5a:d03\", \"start\": 278, \"end\": 364, \"text\": \"The album includes Tower of Power's horn section, and Stevie Wonder's ex-wife Syreeta.\"}, \"D4S5\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0275-408b1741bd5a:d03\", \"start\": 365, \"end\": 493, \"text\": \"Its only single release was the Earth, Wind & Fire-inspired \\\"You Need To Be Loved\\\", which has a saxophone solo by Lenny Pickett.\"}, \"D4S6\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0275-408b1741bd5a:d03\", \"start\": 494, \"end\": 607, \"text\": \"Executive producer: Be